        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5c72d77e-e725-5ca4-ba14-01349cd3a33e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mary Tarrero-Serrano, Carlos Prío, Fulgencio Batista, Osvaldo Farrés\n- Roles: Cuban President, Cuban First Lady\n- Places: Cuba\n- Events: Batista's military coup, Cuban Revolution\n- Works: “Quizás, Quizás, Quizás”\n\nFacts:\n- Fulgencio Batista was born as Rubén Zaldívar on January 16, 1901.\n- Fulgencio Batista served as the elected President of Cuba from 1940 to 1944.\n- Mary Tarrero-Serrano was the second wife of Cuban President Carlos Prío.\n- Fulgencio Batista overthrew Carlos Prío in a military coup in 1952.\n- Fulgencio Batista ruled Cuba as a U.S.-backed dictator from 1952 to 1959.\n- Fulgencio Batista was overthrown during the Cuban Revolution in 1959.\n- Osvaldo Farrés received help and inspiration for the lyrics of “Quizás, Quizás, Quizás” from Cuban First Lady Mary Tarrero-Serrano.\n- Fulgencio Batista died on August 6, 1973.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
